{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy","id":1477646,"title":"Adjusting the Dark Ages setting to prevent the rise of the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-29T14:49:39-07:00","id":1477646,"title":"Adjusting the Dark Ages setting to prevent the rise of the Technocracy","content":"Recently (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476937-time-travel-to-wipe-out-the-technocracy\">here</a>) I posted a topic to discuss the scenario of a time-traveling group of mages (and possibly other allied supernaturals) that travel to the past to prevent the Technocracy from existing, since in the present (setting hack) it intensified its persecution of Reality Deviants and expanded it to the other supernatural splats, unleashing an Apocalyptic war between Triatic uber-factions that threatened to destroy the world. I am interested to discuss the same scenario (changing the Dark Ages setting so that the rise of the Technocracy is averted) from the perspective of Dark Ages characters. This might be the result of time-travelers subtly changing the past without an overt intervention, or DA supernaturals following a similar path by a natural timeline divergence. As far as I am concerned, this primarily concerns Tradition mages and fae, although it may also affect vampires and werewolves as convenient.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, there are a few key flashpoints that may be good for this purpose. One obvious possibility is to make the Craftmasons at Mistridge lose and be crushed. In all likelihood, it would cause the faction to be disbanded or destroyed, and without their role, chances are the Order of Reason never gets organized. Another possibily is to bomb the 997 Gathering of the Square that set up the Craftmasons and their nascent alliance with other proto-Order of Reason groups in the first place, although that seems less easy to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Yet another option is to have House Tremere destroyed before or soon after it turns to vampirism. This might happen because their attempt to destabilize the Order of Hermes with the Schism War is discovered and they are singled out as the rogue House instead of the Diedne, and Marched. From my PoV, this would also have the significant option that the Diedne thrive and stay an integral part of the OoH, leading to improved relations with the Old Faith, other 'pagan' Fellowships, and the fae. Alternaitvely, their turn to vampirism is discovered before they had a real chance to adapt Awakened magic to blood sorcery (or Tremere to Diablerize the Salubri Antedeluvian), allowing the OoH to destroy them with ease.<br /> <br /> In all likelihood, if the OoH does not have the face the major distraction and attrition of the First Massasa War, they would notice the potential threat of the Craftmasons and crush them with relative ease. OTOH, a Cainite society without the Tremere Clan may evolve in ways that I find difficult to fathom.<br /> <br /> Not directly related to the Technocracy issue, but it might also be good for Tradition mages to find ways to tone down inter-Fellowship hostility and achieve some kind of cooperation between Fellowships not unlike the Council of Traditions even without the Order of Reason threat as a unifying element, devise appropriate magitech replacement for advanced technology, and prevent Commoners from becoming a serious threat to supernaturals. For the purpose of this scenario, supernaturals staying or becoming the ruling elites of the world is supposed to be a neutral to good thing, within reasonable limits of course. Something like a repeat of the Impergium is bad, but having a functional magocracy or necrocracy is fine.<br /> <br /> As it concerns the fae, I suppose preventing a restart of the fratricidal War of Seasons is likely warranted. Getting rid of the Technocracy likely does away with the rise of Banality, although it may not suffice. I am not sure what vampires or werewolves may need.<br /> <br /> Yet another potential flashpoint to wipe out the Technocracy may be to destroy the Convention of the White Tower in 1325, although I am concerned by then the nascent Order of Reason had already got too momentum by then for its rise to be disrupted.<br /> <br /> Opinions? Suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-30-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T16:45:27-07:00","id":1477653,"title":"","content":"As mentioned in Guide to the Traditions, keep Genghis Khan alive for another year or two, and the Mongols will likely wreck most of Central and Western Europe, derailing everything. <br /> <br /> Alternately, House Tremere's efforts to frame House Diedne for infernalism in 1003 fails, instead causing the Tremere's vampire experiments to be exposed and the House renounced and mostly destroyed by the rest of the Orders. This means that the Order will not be distracted by war with the Tremere and other vampires in the early 1200s when the Craftmasons use the turmoil of the Albigensian Crusade as cover for their attack on Mistridge. <br /> If you also wanted to try to head off the Albigensian Crusade (or at least try to delay it a few years), you could try preventing the 1208 murder of the papal legate Pierre de Castelnau by one of the Count of Toulouse's men, and then work at keeping the Count and Pope Innocent III's relationship at least non-hostile. Two side effects of this are that the Kingdom of France is less able to extend its influence into the south, even if it still defeats the House of Plantagenet, and likely cuts back on the activities of the Papal Inquisition. But how much the latter impacts the activities of the Shadow Inquisition - ie, the groups in Dark Ages: Inquisition - and the Cabal of Pure Thought - what I refer to as the Illuminated Inquisition for clarity - is anyone's guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T17:41:02-07:00","id":1477655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1477653#post1477653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned in Guide to the Traditions, keep Genghis Khan alive for another year or two, and the Mongols will likely wreck most of Central and Western Europe, derailing everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ogedei, surely. Genghis Khan had already been dead for some years by the time the Mongol invasion of Europe got within spitting distance of Austria (1241, Genghis died 1227). Better make sure that you have someone who has a miracle cure for cirrhosis of the liver, because Ogedei really enjoyed quimus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T18:27:09-07:00","id":1477658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1477655#post1477655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ogedei, surely. Genghis Khan had already been dead for some years by the time the Mongol invasion of Europe got within spitting distance of Austria (1241, Genghis died 1227). Better make sure that you have someone who has a miracle cure for cirrhosis of the liver, because Ogedei really enjoyed quimus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Ogedei. I didn't have the book handy to actually look it up.<br /> <br /> I suppose finding a way to not have the 4th Crusade sack Constantinople would also impact the creation of the Order. How you do it might also keep the Giovani from becoming a clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T23:42:46-07:00","id":1477666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1477653#post1477653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned in Guide to the Traditions, keep Genghis Khan alive for another year or two, and the Mongols will likely wreck most of Central and Western Europe, derailing everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be too damaging for Europe at large for my tastes, since I am an (un-woke) Europhile and two of my preferred Fellowships/Traditions (OoH and the Old Faith/Verbena) are largely rooted in European culture (the other two are the Ecstatics and the Akashics). OTOH, if something like this would pave the way to weaken or cripple Abrahamic organized religion, which I dislike, and pave the way to a major resurgence of Paganism, I'd welcome it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternately, House Tremere's efforts to frame House Diedne for infernalism in 1003 fails, instead causing the Tremere's vampire experiments to be exposed and the House renounced and mostly destroyed by the rest of the Orders. This means that the Order will not be distracted by war with the Tremere and other vampires in the early 1200s when the Craftmasons use the turmoil of the Albigensian Crusade as cover for their attack on Mistridge. </div> </div> </div>I too have singled out this Point of Divergence as one of the main options and a preferred one of mine, also because it would allow House Diedne to survive and stay a major part of the OoH, paving the way to much improved relations and cooperation between the Hermetics and the Old Faith/Verbena.I am just not sure what lack of Clan Tremere would mean for vampire society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you also wanted to try to head off the Albigensian Crusade (or at least try to delay it a few years), you could try preventing the 1208 murder of the papal legate Pierre de Castelnau by one of the Count of Toulouse's men, and then work at keeping the Count and Pope Innocent III's relationship at least non-hostile. Two side effects of this are that the Kingdom of France is less able to extend its influence into the south, even if it still defeats the House of Plantagenet, and likely cuts back on the activities of the Papal Inquisition. But how much the latter impacts the activities of the Shadow Inquisition - ie, the groups in Dark Ages: Inquisition - and the Cabal of Pure Thought - what I refer to as the Illuminated Inquisition for clarity - is anyone's guess. </div> </div> </div>As it concerns this other option, of course I'd welcome anything that would weaken or cripple the Shadow Inquisition, because I'd only relate to the DA:I groups as NPC antagonists to be fought if it is my choice (much like the Technocracy). I lack any sympathy for the Hunter/Inquisitor character concept, and it is often tied to the worst aspects of religion I dislike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-30-2022, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T03:25:31-07:00","id":1477675,"title":"","content":"Funny enough, crushing the Order of Reason might not be enough. There is Muslim/Ottoman reason sect The Court of Sacred Sciences and then The Chinese Dragons. Its heavily implied Order of Reason deliberately caused the Court of Sacred Sciences to crack apart so that they only need to merge with the Chinese Dragons when forming the Technocracy. Without the Order of Reason, the Court of Sacred Sciences and the Chinese Dragons can merge to form a new version of Technocracy and instead of the British Empire, you would have the Ottoman Empire reigning supreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T04:01:28-07:00","id":1477677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1477675#post1477675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny enough, crushing the Order of Reason might not be enough. There is Muslim/Ottoman reason sect The Court of Sacred Sciences and then The Chinese Dragons. Its heavily implied Order of Reason deliberately caused the Court of Sacred Sciences to crack apart so that they only need to merge with the Chinese Dragons when forming the Technocracy. Without the Order of Reason, the Court of Sacred Sciences and the Chinese Dragons can merge to form a new version of Technocracy and instead of the British Empire, you would have the Ottoman Empire reigning supreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, certainly I do not want to remove an Euro-centric Technocracy to raise a Chinese-centric or Muslim-centric one in its place. In all likelihood, given stuff such as the prevalent leaning of those cultures toward brutal authoritarianism, the poor status of women in conservative Islam, and foot binding, chances are these versions of the Technocracy would become even more oppressive in the long term than the original one did. Imperialism and colonialism almost surely are going to stay the same no matter who gets on top.<br /> <br /> OTOH, did the Court of Sacred Sciences and/or the Chinese Dragons (I seem to remember a slightly different name, but it escapes me) look any likely to overcome local opposition by mystical proto-Traditions without external support by the Order of Reason? IIRC, the Whatever Dragons had been losing to Akhashic and Wu Lung opposition before the Western Technocracy intervened. If this be the case, arranging a secondary PoD to make the Court of Sacred Sciences fail does not seem too hard.<br /> <br /> E.g. speaking of the Mongol invasions that were previously mentioned, they hit the Muslim world really hard. Some argue they were a major cause of the Islamic civilization stagnating and going into decline. Instead of letting them wreck Europe, could we assume their rampage would be enough to make the CSS fail, by the original timeline terms or assuming they hit the Middle East even harder in this one for whatever reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-30-2022, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T05:44:25-07:00","id":1477680,"title":"","content":"It has been argued that the Mongol conquests had that effect on Baghdad, Persia/Iran, Russia, and China, with all of them becoming much more insular and culturally conservative in the aftermath. It is probably also a factor in the non-Arab Ottoman Turks becoming the new Caliphate and politically dominating much of the Arab world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T07:55:06-07:00","id":1477684,"title":"","content":"Ironically perhaps, I feel like the creatures most able to detect any such breach in time would be among the least able to directly fight back. Those creatures being vampires. The True Brujah would certainly notice any ripples in time, and the Toreador, Malkavian, and Tzimisce would be likely to notice that things aren't going the way they were supposed to. But Vampires can't go back and fix things, so they'd be more likely to try to set things up to stop people from coming back and undoing all their hard work. Imagine a Convention lab getting blown up by a Vampire who died 600 years earlier, or losing all their funding because someone had set up a sell off from the stock market hundreds of years ago. Ultimately I think the Camarilla and Sabbat would still exist, largely because they are the result of ancient god-like beings trying to make them happen.<br /> <br /> I forgot to mention, I believe the elder vampires of the dark ages would likely view the time travel as a bad thing, even if they knew why it was being done. If you notice, the Technocracy actually furthers the goals of the Camarilla, so the powers behind the Camarilla would not necessarily want to see the Technocracy go, they would simply be trying to shape it into a better tool.<br /> <br /> Since people have been talking about the Tremere a lot, allow me to note that many vampires seem to be strangely okay with the Tremere killing one of their siblings and becoming vampires. There's long been some suggestion that Salot wanted or at least accepted the Tremere diablerie. It makes me wonder if some Vampires might have wanted the Tremere to become vampires, specifically so they wouldn't be mages who could mess with vampiric plans in ways the elders would have trouble fighting against. There are a number of ways I think one could go with this, for example if the Tremere becoming vampires was already a plan to stop the demonic corruption of mages (or slow it down). Perhaps there is a reason that killing the Tremere wouldn't have worked as well (for example, Tremere Wraiths would have worked with the Giovanni to bring about the end times earlier, when the world couldn't have recovered.)<br /> <br /> As far as Changelings go, The technocracy actually has less to do with the rise of banality than you may think. In fact, it was the dreaming starting to float away from the mundane world that caused the increase in banality which led into the paradigms of the early technocrats becoming strong enough for those technocrats to become the most influential will workers in the world. This means that if one could find a way to stop the Sundering, the Technocracy would never rise to ascendancy. However, there are many stories about why the sundering occurred, and no one really knows why it happened when it did. I personally believe the Sundering was a way for the dreaming to protect humanity from a demon invasion through the dreaming. In that scenario, imagine you stop the rise of the technocracy by stopping the sundering, only to begin suffering demon invasions. Really though, that wouldn't be ideal for the demon invaders either, as Fae are immortal and super-powerful spirits themselves, and the dreaming is notoriously difficult to traverse, any demon who actually make it past the Arcadian fae would show up at random times and places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T14:48:54-07:00","id":1477707,"title":"","content":"If you want to disrupt the Cabal of Pure Thought, one avenue might be to work to legitimize the Waldensian heresy/movement, be it either keeping the Third Lateran Council from condemning it, or even trying to play off the conflicts between Pope Alexander III and Emperor Fredrick I of the HRE to have what happened with Lutheranism occur centuries early. Alternately, try to alter a number of the Council's canons to make them more in line with the beliefs of the Celestial Chorus rather than the Cabal of Pure Thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T15:44:56-07:00","id":1477804,"title":"","content":"Canonically the turning point is the fall of Mistridge. Without Grimgroth\u2019s betrayal the magi crush the nascent order of reason there and it doesn\u2019t coalesce into the organization that will spawn the technocracy.<br /> <br /> On a large scale what you have to do is to prevent Tremere to choose vampirism over sphere magic. He was well aware of what would happen to his gift if he was turned and considered the implications for quite a long time before accepting Goratrix\u2019s plan. So I\u2019d Tremere can be convinced magic wasn\u2019t dying and it had just shifted he would have no reason to turn his house into a vampire clan. <br /> Alternatively, you need to combat Grimgroth\u2019s disillusionment with the other magi of Mistridge. If he\u2019s on their side he doesn\u2019t betray them and they defeat the order of reason\u2019s attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T22:52:09-07:00","id":1477834,"title":"","content":"If you want to get the 'good' ending, you might try to stop the horrors of Mistridge so the Craftmasons don't have to. They only became truly hostile to magic as a result of the blatant misuse of magic. Hell, Elder Craftmasons were just straight up Hermetic Magisters. The dispute was one of ideology, not paradigm. Remove the blatant abuse and the zealotry dies away. Something like the Order of Reason may rise (Honestly, the OoH was trying to do something similar anyway so if the OoR didn't the OoH would) but it wouldn't be nearly as violently xenophobic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T19:42:59-07:00","id":1478183,"title":"","content":"Honestly the way the Order of Reason was set up and how they won, undoing it would <u><i><b>RADICALLY</b></i></u> alter the world as we know it. Which I would imagine is a big reason why no one in-universe would do it. Well beyond the Godly amount of Magical Power one would need to do and the Ungodly amount of Paradox that would hit you for that. Paradox that would probably punt you out of existence altogether for that.<br /> <br /> Like both the SoE and the VA wouldn't exist in this world, at least not as we know them. Hell, the Traditions as an organization may not exist as it came into existence as a reaction to the rise of the Order. And by that same token, the modern world as we know it wouldn't exist as the Order of Reason/Technocracy were the ones pushing for Science and Technology and other modern ideas. So our technology would be at least a couple centuries back. And for that matter, it's also likely that many modern ideas wouldn't exist like basic Human Rights or that Racism is a Bad Thing.<br /> <br /> There's also another matter to consider if it's a situation where the Order collapses after the Nine Traditions come into existence, that it's been implied that it didn't actually matter who won the Ascension War as the victor would become a monstrous organization that would dominate the world. In fact, the tragedy of the First Cabal was allowed to happen because the Seers of Chronos received visions of a future where the Traditions and Orders would unify... and lead to an worse timeline. A timeline so bad that the Solificati Mage responsible for it was sending the visions back in time so they could stop him before he could do it even though it would result in the utter destruction of his soul and the near destruction of his Tradition. The Rev Ed VE CB even mentions the VE discovering parallel Earths, including one where the Traditions won and they became the Technocracy but with Magic instead of Science while the Order of Reason are the underdog heroes fighting against their tyranny.<br /> <br /> Because at the end of the day, Mages are people like the rest of us and just as flawed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T19:45:43-07:00","id":1478184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1477677#post1477677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, certainly I do not want to remove an Euro-centric Technocracy to raise a Chinese-centric or Muslim-centric one in its place. In all likelihood, given stuff such as the prevalent leaning of those cultures toward brutal authoritarianism, the poor status of women in conservative Islam, and foot binding, chances are these versions of the Technocracy would become even more oppressive in the long term than the original one did. Imperialism and colonialism almost surely are going to stay the same no matter who gets on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but this here is blatant racism.<br /> <br /> Things were far different in the past and how those regions became how they are now has far more to do with history than with &quot;cultural leanings&quot;, even with European influence actually (for example, the Ottomans change their stance on homosexuality to be far more harsh than it used to be by following France's example at the time).<br /> <br /> On the matter of the change to the past, one option would be to instead of changing the Tremere to eliminate them, intervene to have them accepted by the OoH (and probably not go full on turning every House member into vampires). This would effectively make them not be at war with the OoH and instead be possible allies later on, if not still members. Expelling the Tremere wasn't a given because of turning into vampires, so much so that even after discovery the Hermetics analyzed their case for two years before expelling them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T10:47:02-07:00","id":1478289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1478184#post1478184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but this here is blatant racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't call it racism. I don't think the poster is trying to imply that a technocracy developed from the chinese dragons or the order of sacred sciences would be more authoritarian because the race of the people running it were chinese and/or middle eastern.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm not sure what the word for it would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T12:45:44-07:00","id":1478292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1478289#post1478289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't call it racism. I don't think the poster is trying to imply that a technocracy developed from the chinese dragons or the order of sacred sciences would be more authoritarian because the race of the people running it were chinese and/or middle eastern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. My point was that a technocracy developed by the Chinese Dragons or the Order of Sacred Sciences would almost surely be as oppressive as the one built by the Order of Reason, and quite possibly even more so if at all possible, since the overall historical record of Imperial China or the premodern Muslim world seems even more leaning towards authoritarianism (and poor treatment of women) than premodern Europe, and that would be the cultural background those mages tap when they establish their new world order. As it concerns imperialism/colonialism (and treatment of minorities), I think nothing would really change, since the tendency of successful human groups to indulge in conquest and exploitation of less successful ones seems universal.<br /> <br /> I do not think ethnicity enters the picture at all. The issue concerns history, culture, and ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-09-2022, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T23:46:36-07:00","id":1478331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1478289#post1478289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't call it racism. I don't think the poster is trying to imply that a technocracy developed from the chinese dragons or the order of sacred sciences would be more authoritarian because the race of the people running it were chinese and/or middle eastern.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but straightly said it was because of their culture, which is a component of ethnicity (in addition to lineage and phenotype).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1478292#post1478292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue concerns history, culture, and ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>But history and culture are intertwined with ethnicity, that's why prejudice based on systematic misrepresentation of them is also called racism.<br /> <br /> Their pre-modern history isn't more authoritarian than pre-modern Europe. Pre-modern Europe was quite authoritarian and full of very poor treatment of women, and both pre-modern Muslims and Chinese were far more progressive at times.<br /> <br /> All those cultures varied a lot during the Middle Ages, getting more or less conservative depending on a lot of factors. At distinct points in time and space you would see everything, from full acceptance of homosexuality and transgender to death sentences to anyone caught as such, from a state of equity between genders superior to the actual modern Western World to completely shackling women to a role as essentially house servants and sex slaves.<br /> <br /> Looking at the last 100 years as indicative of how those societies were during the entirety of a thousand years period that ended more than 5 hundred years ago is <b>extremely</b> misleading.<br /> <br /> On a very grossly simplified analysis, during the Middle Ages Europe was actually the most conservative, backwards and authoritarian of the three &quot;societies&quot; in discussion (even grouping them as that is extremely misleading of how each actually worked), for several reasons. China would have more variation in time, and the Muslims were the most stable in this regard as far as we can say that, but the average &quot;progressiveness&quot;, if we can state it as that, was the lowest in Europe, and especially in the Late Middle Ages Europe was significantly more conservative and especially authoritarian than the Ottoman Empire.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that while the fall of Rome negatively affected the complexity of state institutions and balance systems in Europe, the Ottomans and Chinese were in full development of their state administrations. The Chinese had an extremely stable state bureaucracy that could keep administration and law systems working almost seamlessly even during intense political turmoil, and the Ottomans had a hugely well developed independent judiciary that rivaled or surpassed Rome. Their closeness to the Byzantine Empire also helped in giving the Muslims in general and the Ottomans in particular access to Greek and Roman classics and philosophy.<br /> <br /> It is still, as said, a gross simplification. Europe actually started to actually become similar to what we usually think as the Medieval thought already during the 16th century, with the Protestant Reformation and the Counter-Reformation. Similarly, most of our ideas on how &quot;traditional society&quot; works in China and the Middle East (and all of the world, actually) come from relatively recent cultural developments. Foot-Binding in China, for example, only became common among the general populace during the Qing Dinasty, in the 17th century, and the current trend of religious extremism in the Middle East informing politics arose only in the 20th century.<br /> <br /> None of this has much to do directly with the setting as is, as it is just a bunch of fictional bullshit that more or less works for a game. But for discussing options for divergent developments in a public forum, I'll be adamant about how much racist crap is racist crap.<br /> <br /> Which in no way means that the people talking racist crap are doing so consciously or out of malice, racism isn't a personal conviction, it is prejudice born out of systemic misinformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T10:46:59-07:00","id":1478582,"title":"","content":"IMO you can't get rid of the Technocracy. Unless you miraculously popularize an extreme luddite bent in all major religions before, let's say, 1000, technological progress is a pandora's box that you can't control and which will naturally and inevitably lead to the rise of some sort of technocracy as forward thinkers seek to rid the world of dangerous and backwards traditions (and Traditions). <br /> <br /> Also,like, if the ming and qing emperors didn't have a brainfart and close off trade, or the Mughals didn't get their country stolen from them by a british company, then they would've very likely modernized naturally like Europe did in our timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T22:25:43-07:00","id":1478738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1477646-adjusting-the-dark-ages-setting-to-prevent-the-rise-of-the-technocracy?p=1478582#post1478582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO you can't get rid of the Technocracy. Unless you miraculously popularize an extreme luddite bent in all major religions before, let's say, 1000, technological progress is a pandora's box that you can't control and which will naturally and inevitably lead to the rise of some sort of technocracy as forward thinkers seek to rid the world of dangerous and backwards traditions (and Traditions).<br /> <br /> Also,like, if the ming and qing emperors didn't have a brainfart and close off trade, or the Mughals didn't get their country stolen from them by a british company, then they would've very likely modernized naturally like Europe did in our timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't agree completely, I also think something in this line applies.<br /> <br /> You can point to any number of moments that affected the history of the Union-As-Is, but at the end of the day, doing so alone won't change the background that gave the Technocracy so much power. After all, new Mages come all the time, old Mages die (even if not of natural causes in your version). Those events put those organizations in certain positions, but what really impacted them in the long run was their ability to still attract new Awakened, to be relevant as ideas and to gather resources, including Resources.<br /> <br /> How do you answer to the needs of a world that is developing sciences and technology, increasing economic growth, and demands political, social and economic stability )and yes, we have far more political stability today than 1 thousand years ago. Actually more than 30 years ago, easy). How do you modernize the world without the Technocracy, and how the remaining Traditions adapt to a modernizing world?<br /> <br /> Such questions may have answers, but those will greatly impact the resulting setting. And the most probable result is that some other group would simply adapt to fill the ecological role of the Union, so to speak, and mostly end up doing the same they did, and just as authoritarian. Forcing the events into the rise of something less authoritarian than the Union would be the real challenge of any time-traveler, long after getting rid of the Union proper (or maybe even not needing to get rid of them). The option of deescalating the current Union instead of changing the past to create a better near-future is still on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}